"parts":[{"text":"வேங்கை","lemma":"வேங்கை","gloss":"kino tree (Pterocarpus marsupium)"}],"gloss":"Vengai tree"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மாத்தகட்டு","parts":[{"text":"மா","lemma":"மா","gloss":"dark/great"},{"text":"தகட்டு","lemma":"தகடு","gloss":"petal/plate"}],"gloss":"of dark petals"},{"surface":"ஒள்வீ","parts":[{"text":"ஒள்","lemma":"ஒள்","gloss":"bright"},{"text":"வீ","lemma":"வீ","gloss":"blossom/flower"}],"gloss":"bright flowers"},{"surface":"தாய","parts":[{"text":"தாய","lemma":"தாய்தல்","gloss":"scattered/spread"}],"gloss":"scattered on"},{"surface":"துறுகல்","parts":[{"text":"துறுகல்","lemma":"துறுகல்","gloss":"boulder/rock"}],"gloss":"the boulder"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இரும்புலி","parts":[{"text":"இரும்","lemma":"இரும்","gloss":"great/dark"},{"text":"புலி","lemma":"புலி","gloss":"tiger"}],"gloss":"great tiger"},{"surface":"வரிப்புறம்","parts":[{"text":"வரி","lemma":"வரி","gloss":"stripe"},{"text":"புறம்","lemma":"புறம்","gloss":"back"}],"gloss":"striped back"},{"surface":"கடுக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"கடுக்கும்","lemma":"கடுத்தல்","gloss":"resembling"}],"gloss":"resembling"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருங்கல்","parts":[{"text":"பெருங்கல்","lemma":"பெருங்கல்","gloss":"great mountain"}],"gloss":"great mountain","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வைப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"வைப்பு","lemma":"வைப்பு","gloss":"region/land"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the region"},{"surface":"நாடு","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"நாடு","gloss":"country/land"}],"gloss":"country"},{"surface":"கிழவோயே","parts":[{"text":"கிழவோய்","lemma":"கிழவோன்","gloss":"lord (vocative)"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"O lord"}]}],"literal":"In the forest of Veṭci, when hunters chase, / the strong bull of the wild bison, not finding a refuge, / makes the forest gems rise and scattered gold glitter, / as it rushes swiftly through the gardens of the tall mountain. / Possessing the great fame of established victory, / in the ancient, fear-inspiring town named after two sides, / where crores of piled-up wealth were given to you, / hear now of the ruin of Araiyam of long-standing state! / Your father's inheritance fully attained, / O garland-wearing Pulikaḍimāl! / One among your ancestors, with wisdom like yours, / despised the praised poetry of Kalaaththalai, / and the consequence of that indeed, O lord of well-moving chariots, / was that Evvi's ancient lineage perished. And when I said, 'These are / the daughters of the generous-handed Paari,' / please bear with my unclear, poor words, O great lord! / I have sent them away. May your spear conquer! On the mountain slope, / where the dark-trunked Vengai tree has blossomed completely, / its bright flowers with dark petals are scattered on the boulder, / resembling the striped back of a great tiger, / O lord of the country of great mountain regions!","translation":"In the Veṭci forest, when hunters chase it, the strong bull of the wild bison, unable to find a hiding place, rushes swiftly through the garden lands of the tall mountain, kicking up forest gems and making scattered gold glitter. You belong to the ancient, awe-inspiring town named after two sides, possessing the great fame of established victory, where crores of piled-up wealth were given to you. Hear now of the ruin of Araiyam, which had a long-standing status! O Pulikaḍimāl, wearing a luxuriant garland, who fully attained your father's inheritance! One of your ancestors, who possessed wisdom like yours, despised the praised poetry of the poet Kalaaththalai, and the consequence of that act, O lord of well-made chariots, was that the ancient lineage of Evvi perished. When I said, 'These are the daughters of the generous Paari,' please bear with my unclear, poor words, O great lord! I have now sent them away. May your spear always conquer! O lord of the country of great mountain regions, where on the mountain slopes, the dark-trunked Vengai tree has blossomed fully, and its bright, dark-petaled flowers scattered on the boulder resemble the striped back of a great tiger!","modern":"வெட்சி மலர்கள் நிறைந்த காட்டில் வேட்டைக்காரர்கள் துரத்த, தங்குவதற்குப் பாதுகாப்பான இடம் கிடைக்காத காட்டு எருமையின் வலிமையான ஆண் மாடு, காட்டில் உள்ள மணிகள் மேலே எழவும், சிதறிய பொன் துகள்கள் மின்னவும், உயர்ந்த மலைச்சாரல் தோட்டங்களில் வேகமாக ஓடும். வெற்றி நிலைபெற்ற சிறந்த புகழைக் கொண்டு, இரு பிரிவாகப் பெயரிடப்பட்ட அச்சம் தரும் பழமையான ஊரில், பல கோடிப் பொருட்கள் உங்களுக்குக் கொடுக்கப்பட்டன. நீண்ட காலம் நிலைபெற்றிருந்த அந்த அரையத்தின் அழிவைப் பற்றி இப்போது கேட்பாயாக! உன்னுடைய தந்தையின் உரிமைகளை முழுமையாகப் பெற்று, தழைத்த மாலையை அணிந்த புலி கடி மாலே! உன்னைப் போன்ற அறிவுடைய உன்னுடைய முன்னோர்களில் ஒருவன், புகழ் பெற்ற கவிஞரான கழாஅத்தலையாரின் பாடலை இகழ்ந்தான். தேர்களை உடைய தலைவனே, அந்த இகழ்ச்சியின் பயனாகவே வள்ளல் எவ்வியின் பழமையான குடி அழிந்தது. 'இவர்கள் கொடைத்தன்மை மிக்க பாரியின் மகள்கள்' என்று நான் கூறிய தெளிவற்ற எளிய சொற்களைப் பொறுத்துக் கொள்வாயாக, பெருமானே! நான் அவர்களை அனுப்பிவிட்டேன். உன்னுடைய வேல் வெற்றி பெறட்டும்! மலைச்சாரலில் அரும்புகள் இல்லாமல் முழுமையாக மலர்ந்த கரிய அடிமரத்தைக் கொண்ட வேங்கை மரத்தின் அழகிய இதழ்களைக் கொண்ட பிரகாசமான பூக்கள் உதிர்ந்து கிடக்கும் பாறை, பெரிய புலியின் வரியுள்ள முதுகைப் போலத் தோன்றும் பெரிய மலை நாட்டை உடைய தலைவனே!","explanation":"The poet Kapilar is addressing Irungovel (Pulikaḍimāl), a chieftain of the Velir clan, after the chieftain refused to marry the daughters of the deceased patron Paari. Kapilar warns Irungovel by recalling a historical event where one of Irungovel's ancestors insulted the poet Kalaaththalaiyar, which led to the destruction of the ancient city of Araiyam and the decline of the lineage of Evvi. Kapilar asks the chieftain to forgive his 'poor words' in bringing Paari's daughters to him and states that he is now leaving with them. The poem concludes with a vivid description of the chieftain's mountainous country, where the fallen yellow Vengai flowers on a dark boulder resemble a striped tiger. This imagery of the tiger, while describing the landscape, subtly hints at the chieftain's fierce power and the danger of pride.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}